From 03de105cf6442ef264ffe147de4aade21340f1d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 09:59:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] world: dear-congress leans, then adopts; demo tells that
 story

With dear-congress's new food-access proposal, cycles now let real
synthesis drive the plan instead of overriding it:

- Cycle 2+: if dear-congress is leaning toward a proposal that answers a
  current complaint (challenger, 1 of 2 rounds), hold the plan for a
  week instead of adding a fix locally; dear-congress adopts it on the
  next cycle. Status/panel: "leaning toward Grocery delivery (1 of 2)",
  then "+ Grocery delivery, adopted by dear-congress".
- Follow-up tracks the last plan that changed, so after a waiting week
  it still names the plan that hurt the resident.
- Skip the fork simulation when the plan doesn't change (identical).
- Demo runs until two changes land after cycle 1 (live: leaning ->
  adopted -> bus; offline: grocery -> bus), with captions for each path,
  and loads packages from real journals only (synthetic=0) so cycle 1
  doesn't depend on synthetic journals accumulated in dear-congress.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
